                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "actually I have an issue with the treesitter now. Cursor is represented with |\r\nBefore, when I was writing C code like this\r\n```c\r\nvoid main() {|}\r\n```\r\n\r\nPressing enter would do\r\n```c\r\nvoid main() {\r\n  |\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nNow it just does\r\n```c\r\nvoid main() {\r\n|}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI guess it's an unintended consequence to inserting a literal enter. Is there a way to restore old behavior without compromises?",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">actually I have an issue with the treesitter now. Cursor is represented with |<br>\nBefore, when I was writing C code like this</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-c notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"void main() {|}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">void</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">main</span>() {|}</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Pressing enter would do</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-c notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"void main() {\n  |\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">void</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">main</span>() {\n  |\n}</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Now it just does</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-c notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"void main() {\n|}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">void</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">main</span>() {\n|}</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I guess it's an unintended consequence to inserting a literal enter. Is there a way to restore old behavior without compromises?</p>",
